# Code owners for this repository.
#
# The `main-branch-protection` ruleset sets `require_code_owner_review`, so a
# pull request touching an owned path needs an approval from an owner of that
# path. Without this file that rule matches nothing and is silently inert,
# which is what it was before.
#
# Order matters: the LAST matching pattern wins, so put narrower rules below
# the catch-all rather than above it.
#
# A code owner cannot approve their own pull request. On a single-maintainer
# repository this rule is therefore unsatisfiable by the author, and a release
# PR still merges via the ruleset's admin bypass. It starts doing real work the
# moment a second maintainer exists.

# Everything, unless a narrower rule below claims it.
